          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em group of ideles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+adeles"} ring of adeles
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔸
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{I} = \mathbb{A}^\times \coloneqq GL_1(\mathbb{A})
                  \\,.
          %p
            In classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+theory"} algebraic number theory
            one embeds a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completions"} completions
            at its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+absolute+values"} archimedean absolute values
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
            of several fundamental
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorems"} theorems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Chevalley"} Claude Chevalley
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"} André Weil
            that the situation was improved somewhat if the number field is embedded in a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+product"} restricted product
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completions"} formal completions
            at all of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+values"} absolute values
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adeles"} adeles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} units
            of this ring are called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em ideles
          %p
            When considering the adeles and ideles, it is their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            as much as their algebraic structure that is of interest. Many important results in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            translate into simple statements about the topologies of the adeles and ideles. For example, the finiteness of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal+class+group"} ideal class group
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirichlet+unit+theorem"} Dirichlet unit theorem
            are equivalent to a certain quotient of the ideles being compact and discrete.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Weston"}> Weston, p. 1
            )
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
              of the ring of adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
              is called the
              %em group of ideles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{I}_{\mathbb{Q}} \coloneqq GL_1(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}) = \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^\times
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              via identification with the set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕀
                        %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(x, x^{-1}) \in \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}^2: \; x \in \mathbb{I}_\mathbb{Q}\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}^2
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The topology on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_\mathbb{Q}
              is strictly finer than the subspace topology inherited from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi p
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times \times \prod_p \mathbb{Z}_p^\times
              is a neighborhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕀
                        %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}_\mathbb{Q}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/145452/43208"} here
          %p
            The same definition holds for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+adeles"} ring of adeles
            of any other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+field"} global field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mi K
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{I}_K \coloneqq GL_1(\mathbb{A}_K)
          %p
            or similar. The notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi J
                    %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_K
            is also common.
          #IdeleClassGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo ×
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K^\times \backslash \mathbb{I}_K
                    \=
                    GL_1(K)\backslash GL_1(\mathbb{A}_K)
            %p
              is called the
              %em idele class group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The idele class group, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IdeleClassGroup"}
              %a{:href => "moduli+space+of+bundles#OverCurvesAndTheLanglandsCorrespondence"} moduli space of line bundles
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+curve"} arithmetic curve
              on which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions"} rational functions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+correspondence"} Langlands correspondence
              and in the abelian case of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tamagawa+measures"} Tamagawa measures
          %p
            The idele class group is a key object in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+field+theory"} class field theory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ProductFormula Product formula
          %p
            Recall the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+norm"} p-adic norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert -\vert}_p
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mfrac
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi ℓ
                      %mo |
                    %mi p
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi ℓ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\left \vert \frac{a}{b}p^\ell \right \vert}_p
                  \\coloneqq
                  p^{-\ell}
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
            coprime to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            one writes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert -\vert}_\infty
          %p
            and associates with the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/place+at+infinity"}> prime at infinity
            ”. When an index runs over the set of all primes (“finite primes”) union with the “prime at infinity” one usually writes it “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            ” instead of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p This induces:
          #IdeleNorm.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em idele norm
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert -\vert} \colon \mathbb{I}_{\mathbb{Q}} \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}^\times
            %p is the function given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi v
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert \alpha\vert} \coloneqq \underset{v}{\prod} {\vert \alpha_v\vert}_v
                    \\,.
          %p
            Notice that by construction there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}^\times \to \mathbb{I}_{\mathbb{Q}}
          #ProductFormula.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (product formula)
            %p
              The idele norm, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IdeleNorm"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}^\times
              inside the ideles, in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\alpha \in \mathbb{Q}^\times \to \mathbb{I}_{\mathbb{Q}})
                    \\;\Rightarrow\;
                    {\vert \alpha\vert}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{v}{\prod} {\vert \alpha_v\vert}_v
                    \= 1
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The product formula, prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductFormula"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IdeleClassGroup"}
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Garrett11"} Garrett 11, section 1
          %h3#StrongApproximationTheorem Strong approximation theorem for the idele class group
          #StrongApproximationTheorem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (strong approximation form ideles)
            %p
              The idele class group, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IdeleClassGroup"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo \
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi p
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                      %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Q}^\times \backslash \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^\times
                    \\simeq
                    (0,\infty)
                    \\times
                    \\underset{p}{\prod}
                    \\mathbb{Z}_p^\times
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoldfeldHundley11"} Goldfeld-Hundley 11, prop. 1.4.5 and below (2.2.7)
          %p
            This implies that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+adeles"} ring of adeles
            may be decomposed into a rational and an idele class factor as:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi 𝔸
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo ×
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo ×
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo ×
                          %mo \
                          %msubsup
                            %mi 𝔸
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %munder
                            %mo ∪
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo ∈
                              %msup
                                %mi ℚ
                                %mo ×
                          %mi n
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo ×
                          %mo \
                          %msubsup
                            %mi 𝔸
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^\times
                  \&amp; \simeq
                  \\mathbb{Q}^\times
                  \\times
                  (\mathbb{Q}^\times \backslash \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^\times)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\underset{n \in \mathbb{Q}^\times}{\cup}
                  n \cdot
                  (\mathbb{Q}^\times \backslash \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^\times)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoldfeldHundley11"} Goldfeld-Hundley 11, prop. 1.4.6 and below (2.2.7)
          %p
            This decomposition is crucial in the discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            (see there) as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adelic+integral"} adelic integral
          %h3#automorphic_forms_and_relation_to_dirichlet_characters Automorphic forms and Relation to Dirichlet characters
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphic+forms"} automorphic forms
            of the idele group are essentially
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirichlet+characters"} Dirichlet characters
            in disguise (
            %a{:href => "#GoldfeldHundley11"}> Goldfeld-Hundley 11, below def. 2.1.4
            )
          %h3#FunctionFieldAnalogy Function field analogy
          %p
            Via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            one may understand any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field"} function field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions"} rational functions
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+curve"} arithmetic curve
