              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            has the interpretation of being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+functions"} ring of functions
            on all punctured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disks"} formal disks
            around all points of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Frenkel05"} Frenkel 05, section 3.2
          %p
            This means for instance that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_n(\mathbb{A}_F)
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+adeles"} ring of adeles
            has the interpretation as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycles
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+vector+bundles"} algebraic vector bundles
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
            with respect to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of that curve by the complement of a finite number of points together with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disks"} formal disks
            around these points. Here for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1(\mathbb{A}_F)
            is the group of ideles.
          %p
